Root run_workbench.sh launcher v2. Resolve repository from script location. Build TypeScript/physics-workbench in unique external cache snapshot using offline npm pinned lockfile, optional explicit installed WORKBENCH_NODE_MODULES. Build actual gateway via offline locked Cargo with external CARGO_TARGET_DIR, then exec loopback service exposing only read-only repo and books roots. No source-tree generated output, provider calls, server stop or commits. Default cache XDG_CACHE_HOME or HOME/.cache/mathphysics-workbench; support WORKBENCH_CACHE_DIR, WORKBENCH_FRONTEND_DIR, WORKBENCH_BOOK_ROOT, WORKBENCH_PORT, --port N and --build-only. Cache must be outside repository. Missing frontend/books/dependencies fail clearly. Built frontend snapshot kept for running service. Parent integrates frontend separately. Independent verification: bash -n and actual --build-only smoke test with staged frontend and cached node_modules. Full PDD generation unverified.

Approved refinement: default books root is ONLY Physics/Srednicki-QuantumFieldTheory under workspace Data/Public/books, optional if absent with visible notice. Always use mathphysics root ID, books ID only when available. WORKBENCH_NPM_OFFLINE defaults1; only explicit0 permits online npm ci, installs remain external cache. Never silently retry online. Missing frontend/dependencies still fail clearly.

Standalone Explore integration: WORKBENCH_APP=explore selects Vite game-only entry and skips notebook/PDF assets; copy output explore.html to index.html before serving so the independent launcher starts directly in the game. Default notebook launch still builds notebook+optional independent Explore entry. Both use shared Rust services; neither needs the other app running.
